HSRP Operation

Each VLAN has three gateway addresses:

.1 = HSRP Virtual IP
.2 = R2 physical gateway address
.3 = R3 physical gateway address

For example, VLAN 10 uses:

HSRP VIP: 192.168.10.1
R2:       192.168.10.2
R3:       192.168.10.3

Hosts use the HSRP Virtual IP as their default gateway:

Default Gateway: 192.168.10.1

R2 has a priority of 110 while R3 has a priority of 100, making R2 the preferred Active router.

The preempt command allows R2 to reclaim the Active role after recovering.

